WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.447
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.447 --> 00:00:14.462
Today, success levels: how a roll turns into what actually happens.

5
00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:17.954
Open Mechanics, then Success Levels.

6
00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:20.970
When the engine rolls a skill check it gets a score,

7
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.275
and these bands decide which outcome that score lands in,

8
00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:26.885
from critical failure up to critical success.

9
00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:30.467
First successful tier is where success starts.

10
00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:35.984
That band and every band above it count as a success, and everything below fails.

11
00:00:35.984 --> 00:00:38.300
Voyage starts it at mixed results.

12
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:43.612
Open a band. The name is what players see, and it's also what triggers look for,

13
00:00:43.612 --> 00:00:47.428
so rename one and any trigger using the old name stops working.

14
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:52.170
Minimum and maximum score are the band's range, both included.

15
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.056
The bands have to fit together with no gaps or overlaps,

16
00:00:56.056 --> 00:01:00.498
and the top band has no maximum, so every score lands somewhere.

17
00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:07.028
And narration instructions are the note handed to the narrator when an action lands in this band.

18
00:01:07.028 --> 00:01:11.615
I kept Voyage's bands and gave the two critical ones a bit of our circus.

19
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.001
Where does the score come from?

20
00:01:15.001 --> 00:01:21.327
The skill, the attribute, a random roll and any modifiers, added up, minus how hard the action is.

21
00:01:21.327 --> 00:01:27.071
Early in a game there's a ten point bonus on top, so a new character gets a softer start.

22
00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.067
That's success levels.

23
00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.977
Our bands are linked in the description.

24
00:01:32.977 --> 00:01:38.869
Next time, the advanced mechanics: levelling up, death, combat and relationships.

25
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:43.281
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

